{"kft": [{"id": "kft", "headword": "कृत्", "headword_slp1": "kft", "fold": "kft", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "कृत् (I) vt. 6P (pp. कृत्त; pres. कृंतति) 1. To cut, to cut off, to divide, to tear asunder, to destroy, प्रहरति विधिर्मर्मच्छेदी न कृंतति जीवितम् M.M.ix., M.viii.12, Bt.xvi.15, ix.42, xv.97.With अव-, to cut off, to tear asunder, to divide.With उद्-, 1. to tear out, उत्क्रियोत्कृत्य कृतिम् M.M.v.; 2. to cut off, R.xii.49.With नि-, to cut off, to tear off, निकृंतान्निव मानसम् Bt.vii.11, भल्लनिकृत्तकंठैः R.vi.58.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "कृत् (II) vt. 7P (pp. कृत्त) 1. To surround; 2. to spin.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "कृत् (I) a. (generally at the end of compounds) doer, maker, performer, manufacturer, composer &c. See Bg.xv.15, M.i.18.", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "कृत् (II) m. 1. An affix used to form nouns from roots; 2. a noun formed by a Kṛt affix.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}, {"id": "kFt", "headword": "कॄत्", "headword_slp1": "kFt", "fold": "kft", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "कॄत् vt. 10U (pp. कीर्तित; pres. कीर्तयति-ते) 1. To name, to mention, R.i.87, M.vii.167; 2. to commemorate, to praise, e.g. भ्रातुरचिकीर्तश्च विक्रमम् Bt.xv.72.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "kfta": [{"id": "kfta", "headword": "कृत", "headword_slp1": "kfta", "fold": "kfta", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vaidya", "senses": [{"gloss": "कृत (I) a. (f. ता) Done, performed, made, manufactured, (pp. of कृत् q.v.)", "gloss_language": "en"}, {"gloss": "कृत (II) n. 1. Work, deed, movement, M.vii.197; 2. service, benefit; 3. consequence, result; 4. name of that side of a die which is marked with four points; 5. name of the first of the four Yugas of the world extending over 17,28,000 years of men, See M.i.69, and Kull. on it; 6. the number ‘4.’", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["कृतं"], "synonyms_slp1": ["kftaM"]}, {"id": "kftA", "headword": "कृता", "headword_slp1"